--TEST--
A `Core\Csv::rows` walk that a child task returns names no reader in the task that receives it, so reading it there stops the program and never reaches the task's own walk at the same position
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Csv::rows
// A task returns a CSV walk, and reading it outside the task stops the program.
// Before that, the program's own walk reads its own file.

Core\IO\File $out = Core\IO::open("own.csv", Core\IO::FileMode::Write);
$out->write("own,row\n");
$out->close();
Core\IO\File $in = Core\IO::open("own.csv", Core\IO::FileMode::Read);
var $own = Core\Csv::rows($in);

var $result = Core\Task::all({
    rows: fn (): Core\Csv\Rows<string> => {
        Core\IO\File $out = Core\IO::open("task.csv", Core\IO::FileMode::Write);
        $out->write("task,row\n");
        $out->close();
        return Core\Csv::rows(Core\IO::open("task.csv", Core\IO::FileMode::Read));
    },
});
foreach ($own as array<string> $record) {
    echo "own: ", $record[0], "\n";
}
foreach ($result->rows as array<string> $record) {
    echo "this line does not run\n";
}
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.fs]
read = ["."]
write = ["."]
--EXPECT--
own: own
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
FATAL: A `Core\Csv\Rows` walk was read in a task other than the one that called `Core\Csv::rows`. A walk works only in that task.
